{"id":48,"date":"2011-09-13T17:09:32","date_gmt":"2011-09-13T17:09:32","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/drumsandelectronics.wordpress.com\/?p=48"},"modified":"2021-01-06T12:21:57","modified_gmt":"2021-01-06T12:21:57","slug":"equipment-standard-preamp","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/equipment-standard-preamp\/","title":{"rendered":"Equipment standard (preamp)"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.mandalay.no\/main\/wp-content\/uploads\/2013\/05\/9-1-e1368527665422.jpg\"><img data-attachment-id=\"1718\" data-permalink=\"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/equipment-standard-preamp\/9-1-2\/\" data-orig-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/9-1-e1368527665422.jpg?fit=586%2C108&amp;ssl=1\" data-orig-size=\"586,108\" data-comments-opened=\"0\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"9-1\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-medium-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/9-1-e1368527665422.jpg?fit=300%2C55&amp;ssl=1\" data-large-file=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/9-1-e1368527665422.jpg?fit=586%2C108&amp;ssl=1\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-full wp-image-1718 aligncenter\" alt=\"9-1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.mandalay.no\/main\/wp-content\/uploads\/2013\/05\/9-1-e1368527665422.jpg?resize=586%2C108\" width=\"586\" height=\"108\" srcset=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/9-1-e1368527665422.jpg?w=586&amp;ssl=1 586w, https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/9-1-e1368527665422.jpg?resize=300%2C55&amp;ssl=1 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 586px) 100vw, 586px\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>I had to see if I could settle with the equipment I now have and move on to the next phase, or if I needed to invest in better and more expensive equipment. <a href=\"http:\/\/www.lydrommet.no\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lydrommet<\/a> were kind enough to borrow me an <a href=\"http:\/\/focusrite.com\/products\/mic_pres\/isa828\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ISA 828<\/a> preamp to do some testing.<\/p>\n<p>I tested the <a href=\"http:\/\/focusrite.com\/products\/mic_pres\/isa828\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ISA 828<\/a> up against the preamps in a <a href=\"http:\/\/focusrite.com\/products\/audio_interfaces\/saffire_pro_40\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Focusrite pro40<\/a>, they are from the same manufacturer, but the pro 40 costs <a href=\"http:\/\/www.musiciansfriend.com\/pro-audio\/focusrite-saffire-pro-40-firewire-interface\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">500$<\/a> and the ISA 828 costs <a href=\"http:\/\/www.musiciansfriend.com\/pro-audio\/focusrite-isa-828-8-channel-mic-pre-amp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2500$ <\/a>(september 13th 2011).<\/p>\n<p>I connected the ISA 828 to the Pro40&#8217;s ADAT-input and recorded Kick drum, Snare drum and over heads, first with one preamp, then the other one. I see now that I should have had an xlr-split and recorded with both preamps to two different tracks at the same time to get a more scientifically correct comparison, but at the end, I got what I came for.<\/p>\n<p>Listen for your self:<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Kick drum (recorded with AKG C 547 BL):<\/p>\n<p>Pro40:<br \/>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23250090&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>ISA828:<br \/>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23250054&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Snare drum (recorded with AKD C 518):<\/p>\n<p>Pro40 (stick):<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23251177&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>ISA828 (stick):<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23251134&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Pro40 (brushes):<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23251203&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>ISA828 (brushes):<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23251158&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Overhead (recorded with AKG C 414):<\/p>\n<p>Some out-of-phase-ish issues here, caused by soundcloud.<\/p>\n<p>Pro40:<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23252868&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>ISA828:<\/p>\n<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"166\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"no\" src=\"https:\/\/w.soundcloud.com\/player\/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fapi.soundcloud.com%2Ftracks%2F23252803&width=false&height=false&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&visual=false&show_comments=false&color=false&show_user=false&show_reposts=false\"><\/iframe>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>Everything was recorded at 48.0 kHz and 24bit.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>.<\/p>\n<p>At a small PA system (mackie) I couldn&#8217;t hear the difference between the Pro40 and the ISA828 in any of the above examples, but when I got home to my studio monitors I heard some differences on the Over heads recordings and on the Brushes recordings.<\/p>\n<p>My live performances are not intended to be played with studio monitors and the difference I heard on my studio monitors is, in my particular case, and by my opinion, not worth 2000$.<\/p>\n<p>It is good to know that I find the Pro40&#8217;s preamps good enough for my usage, It&#8217;s latency and LLP (Low Latency Performance) on the other hand is a challenge I&#8217;ll address later.<\/p>\n<a id=\"pd_a_5500471\"><\/a><div class=\"CSS_Poll PDS_Poll\" id=\"PDI_container5500471\" style=\"\"><\/div><div id=\"PD_superContainer\"><\/div><noscript><a href=\"https:\/\/polldaddy.com\/p\/5500471