etween when an audio signal enters and when it emerges from a system. Potential contributors to latency in an audio system include analog-to-digital conversion,\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/12\/latencyheader_l.jpg?fit=700%2C512&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":85,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/23\/equipment-standard-microphones-triggering\/","url_meta":{"origin":48,"position":2},"title":"Equipment standard (Microphones &#8211; triggering)","date":"September 23, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"Lydrommet were also kind enough to lend me some microphones. I tested them with the same intent as I tested the preamps, I wanted to see if there was any reason for me to invest in other microphones. I already have this one in all my drums: Also I have\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?fit=494%2C1200&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":749,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2012\/01\/15\/dancer-controlling-sound-with-sensors-idea-sketch\/","url_meta":{"origin":48,"position":3},"title":"Dancer controlling sound with sensors &#8211; Idea sketch","date":"January 15, 2012","format":false,"excerpt":"(...) a sensor based setup for a dancer and a drummer, where the dancer can pick up sounds played by the drummer and process them with movement (...) My project description What: Dancer wearing sensors - controlling sound. The idea is that the dancer can approach my drum set (sound\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2012\/01\/lydplukking-e1368445521324.jpg?fit=896%2C1200&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height"